From 27b45236d779f92913045af5c3e13a4d40e95f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: a <a@b.c>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:41:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nintendo-tera: add MCU core

Add the transport-agnostic Nintendo Switch controller MCU core as a new
module. It implements the MCU protocol -- mode/state control, config and
data packets, status polling, and the 0x31 MCU-input dispatch that feeds
the IR and NFC sub-features -- entirely through a small transport
interface (nintendo-tera.h): ->send_subcmd (output 0x01 with ack, taking
an optional content-based ack matcher), ->send_raw (MCU data packets and
raw output reports; the transport fills packet_num and the rumble
passthrough), a struct device for logging, and the transport's output
mutex.

The IR (nintendo-tera-ir) and NFC (nintendo-tera-nfc) feature files are
added in the following commits; joycon_tera_probe() brings them up when
their config options are enabled. The hid-nintendo and joycon-serdev
transport drivers are wired to this core in later commits.
